  "scope": {
    "native": "Current automatic native selection. Same synthetic RGBA16F/RG16F zero-motion, model, controls,8 blocks,1 pass. PNNP order;2 processes/route/extent,128 frames each,discard32;mean of process medians. GPU interval excludes uploads/readbacks. Stock clocks observed, not locked. Arithmetic mean of two process medians. Native CUDA kernel selection is current, not the earlier diagnostic baseline.",
    "portable": "Per-row dates, process counts and motion/reset fixture are authoritative. Latest CUDA/Vulkan RTX use fractional-motion temporal history; latest CPU/HIP use reset frames. SYCL CPU/Vulkan AMD retain earlier temporal timings. Medians of process medians; full call includes host preparation, transfers, inference, resolve and broker overhead, excluding startup/file I/O. Native uses a different fixture and boundary. Offline timings, not game FPS.",
    "memory": "Process host commitment, working set, and owned allocations are overlapping scopes, not quantities to add. Native DXGI residency includes the benchmark harness. Portable graph allocation bytes are provider-owned buffer requests, not whole-process GPU residency.",
    "validation": "Saved Phoenix regression hashes plus direct NVIDIA reset/final comparison on native fixture. Portable output hashes checked on saved fixtures and repeated history sequences across processes. No claim of portable/native identical output or live-game FPS.",
    "host_memory": "Whole-probe observations, not matched runner-only RAM. Phoenix retains weight/fixture host caches through the loop; NVIDIA uses transient host upload planes. Private commit and working set overlap GPU/driver allocations."
  },
